    {
      "id": 13244,
      "name": "The Burning Stickman",
      "username": "The_Burning_Stickman",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/the_burning_stickman/{size}/2003_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-07-03T21:10:56.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>So, just out of my own curiosity, what do you all consider the worst card for a given villain to flop on the first turn? The one that comes down and immediately signals a game that's going to be, at best, hard as hell on you and at worst, all but unwinnable?</p><p>For me, the first that comes to mind is Profane Summons with Apostate. The first time we played against him, he flopped that and pulled out the Runes of Malediction, Tome of the Unknowable, and the Orb of Delirium -- we won, but it was painful starting out since we all needed cards to do anything.</p><p>The second is Ravage from Plague Rat -- having four out of five heroes punching themselves in the face from the start before you have the cards out to mitigate it is rough.</p><p>What about y'all?</p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:59.341Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 2,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 10.0,
